[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d086598-d0f7-52ac-bba9-a6017b092d64"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d086598-d0f7-52ac-bba9-a6017b092d64" :question/id #uuid "8d086598-d0f7-52ac-bba9-a6017b092d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-21051" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c85e6ee974a59d956367634fdd1d57b65e9d42a980fe1750886527b173f05d32.png)\n\nFind $BM$ given that the area of $△ACB$ is $49\\,{cm}^{2},$ $AM=5\\,cm,$ and $MC=9\\,cm.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the height is $h=BM,$ and the corresponding base is \n\n$$\nb=AM+MC=14\\,cm.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the height as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 49 & =\\frac{14\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 98 & =14\\cdot h \\\\ h & =\\frac{98}{14} \\\\ h & =7\\,cm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $BM=7\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8da7771e-63f1-5e10-be3c-1af25ccedf2e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8da7771e-63f1-5e10-be3c-1af25ccedf2e" :answer-field/id #uuid "8da7771e-63f1-5e10-be3c-1af25ccedf2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-897c0883-8ea7-5679-b872-375f1438d23b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68718dec-ecd8-5ae5-a90a-23ccd4586c90" "answer-b854d192-b8ff-551c-8ab1-aef38e4dfe2b" "answer-498f62c4-d10e-5980-af7b-cf193748dc55" "answer-2ed3ec42-7887-59f4-8607-49a2c72ca3d0" "answer-897c0883-8ea7-5679-b872-375f1438d23b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68718dec-ecd8-5ae5-a90a-23ccd4586c90" :answer/id #uuid "68718dec-ecd8-5ae5-a90a-23ccd4586c90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10